# chat at 12x60 (the flat tier, TUI-DESIGN-2 §4.1): JEVCODE_MOCK_INTAKE=ambiguous — the narrow terminal gets the same
# conversational answer as the wide one: the reply, then the `do it` offer, no card and no blocked composer. The quiet
# start (2026-09) prints no `[sandbox]` item in the TUI, so the attached host is read from the status row's `sess $…`
# badge — the controller pushes the session meter in the same breath (`pushSessionSpend`).
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.3
send the date parsing
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
expect make that a task
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
